```

`_fetchOnce` catches everything — returns null for no adapter, unknown on error/timeout. So `refresh` itself effectively never throws... except: `putIfAbsent` with an async closure. Note `Map.putIfAbsent` calls the closure synchronously up to its first await; the returned future is what's stored. `refresh` returns the future. Can it complete with an error? `_fetchOnce` never throws (catch-all + adapter null check). `_changes.add(null)` — a broadcast StreamController's `add` doesn't throw even without listeners. So `refresh` never errors in practice. The `.catchError` in QuotaStore.confirmEndpoint is belt-and-braces; `unawaited(quotas!.refresh(mark))` in the picker without catchError is therefore fine (matches `_kick`'s defensive catchError style, though). Minor inconsistency only.

